violations.fixPrompt:
In `supabase/functions/admin/index.ts`, the per-IP lockout counter in the `fails` map is never invalidated when the lockout window expires, so a stale `n >= MAX_FAILS` causes every later wrong passcode to immediately re-lock the IP.

After the existing check `if (rec && rec.until > now) return bad('too many attempts, try again shortly', 429);`, treat an expired record as invalid. For example, compute an effective previous count that resets once the window has passed:

```ts
const rec = fails.get(ip);
if (rec && rec.until > now) return bad('too many attempts, try again shortly', 429);
// An expired lockout invalidates the counter — start the next window fresh.
const prevFails = rec && rec.until !== 0 && rec.until <= now ? 0 : (rec?.n ?? 0);
```

Then use `prevFails` instead of `rec?.n ?? 0` when incrementing in the wrong-passcode branch: `const n = prevFails + 1;`. Keep the existing `fails.delete(ip)` on success. Do not change the passcode comparison or any other behaviour.

