violations.fixPrompt:
In `supabase/functions/admin/index.ts`, the module-level `fails` map (line 24) never evicts entries, so records from IPs that never authenticate successfully accumulate for the instance's lifetime.

Add a cheap opportunistic sweep of expired records. For example, inside the request handler right after `const now = Date.now();`, occasionally prune entries whose lockout window has elapsed:

```ts
// Opportunistic sweep so one-off IPs don't accumulate for the instance's lifetime.
if (fails.size > 1000) {
  for (const [k, v] of fails) if (v.until <= now) fails.delete(k);
}
```

Alternatively, store a `seen` timestamp on each record and evict entries older than a few multiples of `LOCK_MS`. Keep the existing lockout semantics and the `fails.delete(ip)` on successful passcode unchanged.

